---

📊 26. Measures of Central Tendency

Mean

Average value of the dataset.

Formula

\[
\text{Mean}=\frac{\text{Sum of Values}}{\text{Number of Values}}
\]

Example

Marks = 10, 20, 30

Mean = (10 + 20 + 30) / 3 = 20


---

Median

Middle value after sorting.

10, 20, 30, 40, 50

Median = 30


---

Mode

Most frequently occurring value.

10, 20, 20, 30

Mode = 20


---

📉 27. Measures of Dispersion

Range

Range = Highest Value − Lowest Value


---

Variance

Measures how far values are spread from the mean.


---

Standard Deviation

Square root of the variance.

Small Standard Deviation → Values are close to the mean.

Large Standard Deviation → Values are widely spread.



