📌 Exam Summary

NumPy is a fast and efficient library for numerical computing and array operations.

Indexing & Slicing: Access and manipulate array elements efficiently.

Array Manipulation: Use reshape(), flatten(), ravel(), transpose(), concatenate(), vstack(), hstack(), column_stack(), hsplit(), and vsplit().

Sorting: Use sort() and argsort() to organize data.

Broadcasting & Vectorization: Perform fast operations without explicit loops.

Mathematical Functions: sqrt(), exp(), sin(), cos(), dot(), and arithmetic functions.

Statistical Functions: mean(), median(), sum(), min(), max(), var(), std(), and corrcoef().

EDA: Helps understand, clean, visualize, and analyze datasets before Machine Learning.

Statistics: Uses measures of central tendency (Mean, Median, Mode) and dispersion (Range, Variance, Standard Deviation) to summarize and interpret data.



